==Battleground==
*1 [[Angelic Sleipnir]] spawns.
*Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
*1 [[Relic Doge]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Bore]] spawns as the boss.
**2 [[Shy Boy]]s spawn, delay 0.67 seconds<sup>20f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Relic Doge]]s spawn, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
**3 [[Metal Doge]]s spawn, delay 0.67 seconds<sup>20f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 80% HP:
**1 [[Gentleman Bros. (Enemy)|Gentleman Bros.]] spawns as the boss.
**15 [[Metal Doge]]s spawn, delay 2~2.67 seconds<sup>60f~80f</sup>.
**1 [[Loris]] spawns.
**1 [[Bun Bun Black]] spawns.
**4 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn, delay 2~4 seconds<sup>60f~120f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This floor is very similar to the original [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 19|Floor 19]], and subsequently, [[Satan's Bedroom]]. The beginning is the same, aside from having one Relic Doge, and the first wave is the same, except oddly the Bore is actually weaker by 50% mag, and infinitely spawning Relic Doges will start spawning in place of [[I.M. Phace|I.M. Phace]]. The last wave has changed quite a bit however, [[Director Kurosawah]] has been replaced by Gentleman Bros, even more Relic Doges, and a Loris joins as well. A decent [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitter]] unit should be used to help clear out the Metal Doges, units with [[:Category:Cats with Freeze Immunity|Freeze Immunity]] can be helpful here, [[:Category:Anti-Dark Cats|Anti Darks]], [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|Reds]], and [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|Floatings]] help as well.

